gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.overview=The Electric Blast Furnace is your first electric multiblock, used to blast new materials that require higher heat levels.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.controller_placement=The EBF Controller is placed in the center of the bottom layer's front face.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.hatches_and_casings=The rest of the 3x3 base contains Heat Proof Machine Casings with I/O Buses, I/O Hatches, Energy Hatches, and a Maintenance Hatch.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.heating_coils=Above the base are two layers of Heating Coils, each forming a 3x3 hollow ring.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.hollow_center=The center 1x2x1 space inside the coils must be left hollow for it to be valid.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.top_layer_and_muffler=The top layer is a 3x3 of casings with a Muffler Hatch in the very center to vent pollution.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.gas_recovery=Optionally, you can also add an output hatch on the top layer to capture gas from your muffler hatch.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.rain_protection=Protect your EBF with a roof! Otherwise, your energy hatches will explode upon contact with rain.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.text.operation=Supply power and items, ensure maintenance is fixed, and the EBF will begin blasting!

gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.controller=Place the controller at the front bottom center. Reserve a 3x3 base and room to access the hatches.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.controller=Place the controller
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.base=Install two LV Energy Hatches, a Maintenance Hatch and item I/O Buses. This example also has a fluid Input Hatch; fill the remaining positions with casings.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.base=Complete the base
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.lower_coil=Place eight Cupronickel Coils in a 3x3 ring. Leave the center as air.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.lower_coil=Place the first coil ring
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.upper_coil=Add eight more coils of the same tier. Keep both center blocks clear of torches, cables and pipes.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.upper_coil=Place the second coil ring
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.top=Place an upward-facing Muffler Hatch in the top center. Fill the outer ring with casings or fluid Output Hatches.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.top=Add the top and Muffler Hatch
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.roof=Leave an air block above the Muffler Hatch, then build a roof higher up. Keep pipes, cables and roof blocks away from the vent.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.roof=Keep the vent clear and add a roof
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.text.maintenance=Check the structure at the controller and repair every maintenance issue at the Maintenance Hatch. Verify power and output space before adding ingredients.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.build.label.maintenance=Check the structure and maintenance
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.overview=Build the EBF and steam supply, then power it from four LV turbines through two short branches.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.overview=A short direct connection
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.hatches=Each LV Energy Hatch accepts up to 2A LV. Together they support a 120 EU/t recipe; the external voltage remains LV.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.hatches=Two LV Energy Hatches
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.generators=Use two LV steam turbines for each hatch. Wrench their energy output faces toward the cables. Each turbine outputs at most 1A LV.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.generators=Place four turbines
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.cables=Each branch must carry at least 2A. Keep it short to preserve the small power margin above 120 EU/t.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.cables=Connect two short cable branches
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.steam=Supply steam to all four turbines. Check boiler output, fuel and pipe distribution so none of the turbines runs dry.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.steam=Keep every turbine supplied with steam
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.text.trial=Four turbines provide a nominal 128 EU/t. Repair maintenance, protect the devices from rain and test a small batch through to completion.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.direct.label.trial=Repair maintenance and test a small batch
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.overview=Place an LV Battery Buffer near the EBF. Feed its input sides from the generators and connect its output face to the two hatches.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.overview=A battery-buffer supply
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.generators=This example has eight LV steam turbines and other LV machines. Size the generator-side cables for their combined current.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.generators=Generators and their supply trunk
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.batteries=Put four usable LV batteries in the four-slot buffer and charge them first. With only one battery, its maximum output is only 1A.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.batteries=Install four LV batteries
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.output=Use at least 4A LV capacity on the output trunk and 2A on each hatch branch. Connect the buffer energy output face.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.output=Connect the output face and 4A trunk
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.hatches=The buffer supplies 4A LV; it does not turn the cable into an MV-voltage line. Respect the voltage rating of each hatch.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.hatches=The hatches still receive LV power
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.text.balance=If battery charge falls across successive recipes, average generation is insufficient. Include the EBF, other machines and losses in the power budget.
gregtech.ebf.ponder.buffer.label.balance=Check the long-term energy balance